nodes.body:
Thanks for the guidance. Before I rework the PR, I want to confirm the intended scope and retry boundary.

My plan is to:

- remove RetryPromptFactory from AsyncLLM and keep AsyncLLM responsible only for surfacing MultiModalCacheMissError and cleaning up the failed request;
- initially support the common OpenAI endpoints: /v1/chat/completions, /v1/completions, and /v1/embeddings;
- in each endpoint, retain the source request, catch the cache miss while consuming the engine iterator, rebuild the prompt with skip_mm_cache=True, and resubmit it once imperatively;
- retry only before any response has been emitted; if the retry also misses, return the retryable 503 error;
- leave Responses, batch, beam search, speech-to-text, and scale-out paths out of this PR for now.

Does this match what you had in mind? Also, should /v1/responses be included in the initial set of common endpoints?

